.TH ISOPROPYL 1 "August 2026" "ISOpropyl 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
isopropyl \- safety-focused bootable USB and SD media writer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B isopropyl
.RI [ --portable ]
.RI [ image ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ISOpropyl
is a graphical Linux application for inspecting disk images and writing them
to removable USB and SD media. It supports authenticated raw/DD writes,
filesystem-aware ISO construction, verification, guarded drive tools, and
selected Linux and Windows image downloads.
.PP
Run ISOpropyl as a regular desktop user. Narrow destructive operations are
delegated to a fixed PolicyKit helper. The application refuses to run as root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --portable
Store non-destructive preferences in
.I isopropyl.ini
beside the launcher. Destructive confirmations are never persisted.
.TP
.I image
Open one disk image when the application starts.
.SH SAFETY
Writing an image destroys data on the selected target. Verify the displayed
device path, model, capacity, and serial number. Keep post-write verification
enabled and use expendable media while this release is marked alpha.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/isopropyl-device-helper
Fixed root-owned PolicyKit helper launcher.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/io.github.codebooker.isopropyl.*.policy
Narrow privileged action definitions.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR isopropyl-cli (1),
the installed README, and
.UR https://github.com/codebooker/isopropyl
the ISOpropyl project page
.UE .
